+# A place can keep holding you — 25 September 2026
+
+The map opts into `floor:walk` on the existing Life address study. Its 24×24 floor changes from 0.2 m to 0.4 m pitch, spanning 9.6 m. The floor centre moves from local z=3.6 to 6.8 within the existing front bay. Gold squares, labels, wires and lamps follow their original addresses. The dish, Life solver, presets, eight controls, clock and generation limit are retained. Default address-study placements keep the earlier 4.8 m floor.
+
+The receiver source is included in this review's before snapshot and source manifest. The floor changes colour, with no per-cell collision added or removed. The underlying museum floor supports empty and occupied addresses.
+
+## A second artifact was occupying the floor
+
+Native inspection found the rear hexagonal terrain, radius 20 at 0.5 m hex size, spreading roughly 35 m across. The floor approach hit its colliders. The map now places that work at (9,23) with `display:table`. Its full simulation root is uniformly scaled to 0.12 over a 4.5×4 m table. All 1,261 sites, eleven allocated layers, transition law, random flips and existing colliders remain; the control is separately kept at full scale, 1.4 m high, and the status label compensates the scale. Other placements retain the original display. Its slider operation and complete rear-gallery access need their own review; height and footprint alone are not interaction acceptance.
+
+## TRACE repair
+
+Switching TRACE off previously restored floor colours but left the dish showing the old red/blue wake until an update. The native regression reproduced this. TRACE-off now calls the existing display refresh before the shared refresh; neither buffer nor generation changes.
+
+## Evidence
+
+41 native checks pass with 14 actual desktop pointer events. These include the four-generation glider translation, unchanged 576 floor transforms, shared colours, TRACE on/off, blinker centre, LINK and onset counts, a meeting empty at generation 6, replay, RUN, the 48-generation limit and default-display compatibility.
+
+A supplied museum CharacterBody walks to empty A=(10,10), remains supported when it becomes occupied at generation 8, and stays in place when it empties at generation 12. Its lamp follows the state. Rays at all four floor corners and A find museum-floor support. The body does not write into the Life rule. This is a controlled desktop fixture, not a headset session.
+
+First failed run and pictures remain under `doc/book/iterations/2026-09-25-ca-life-floor/first-native`. The final process exits 0 without GDScript errors; existing UID/resource, registry, environment, renderer and generated-art warnings remain in the log. No tracked-hand, comfort, Quest, full-gallery or learner acceptance is claimed. No solver optimisation was attempted.
+
+The chapter gains a bodily encounter and one original native figure. Existing code excerpts, TRACE passage and critical essay remain. Its hex paragraph now names both the changed neighbourhood and birth condition, the optional random flips and the table staging.
+
+
+Runtime staging note: the museum automatically relocates the same generated dream_bodies sculpture from (11.5, 0.42, 23.5) to (2.5, 0.42, 23.5), clearing the new table footprint. Its rotation and scale are unchanged. All other native roots except the deliberately restaged hex retain their positions. The initial overly broad publication assertion and this explicit comparison are retained as diagnostic-verification.json and runtime-restaging.json.
